## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical APIM quota implementation and OpenAI routing for multi-tenant SaaS architectures.

## Key Concepts
- API Management policies with rate-limit-by-key
- Tenant-scoped routing via request headers
- Telemetry integration with Application Insights

## Code Example
```xml
<policies>
  <inbound>
    <base />
    <set-variable name='TenantID' value='@(context.Request.Headers.GetValueOrDefault("x-tenant-id","default"))' />
    <rate-limit-by-key calls='60' renewal-period='60' key='@(context.Variables["TenantID"])' />
  </inbound>
</policies>
```

```javascript
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant-id'] || 'default';
  const startTime = Date.now();

  try {
    const response = await callOpenAI(req.body);

    // Log usage to Application Insights
    context.log('TenantUsage', {
      tenantId,
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
      duration: Date.now() - startTime,
      status: 'success'
    });

    return { status: 200, body: response };
  } catch (error) {
    context.log.error('TenantError', { tenantId, error: error.message });
    return { status: 500, body: { error: 'Service unavailable' } };
  }
};
```

## Validation Approach
Test with multiple tenant IDs using load testing tools, verify rate limits trigger at 60 requests/minute per tenant, and confirm telemetry appears in Application Insights queries.

## Why This Is Asked

Data provenance in multi-tenant analytics platforms is critical for compliance, cross-tenant data sharing, and debugging lineage issues. This question evaluates the ability to integrate Azure data cataloging services, OpenAI-powered analysis, and per-tenant security controls into a production-grade pipeline.

## Key Concepts

- Data provenance and lineage tracking
- Microsoft Purview for metadata management
- Cognitive Search-powered versioned knowledge base
- Role-based access control (RBAC) with Azure Active Directory
- Data Lake auditing and logging
- Drift detection in ingestion pipelines

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lineage consistency validation
const validateLineage = (event) => {
  return event.source && event.sink && event.transactionId;
};

// Drift detection logic
const detectDrift = (expected, actual) => {
  return expected.source !== actual.source || 
         expected.sink !== actual.sink;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle real-time vs. batch lineage processing?
- What strategies would you use to minimize AI hallucinations when assessing lineage accuracy?
- How would you design the RBAC model to support nested tenant hierarchies?

